#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksudoku; is a sudoku game for &kde; with many variants."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sudoku is a logic-based symbol placement puzzle. The objective is to fill a "
"grid so that each column and each row contains contains each symbols exacly "
"once. Mosty there are other constraints added."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most common sudoku game has a 9x9 grid and uses 1 to 9 as symbols. As "
"extra constraint the grid is devided in 9 3x3 grids which has to contain all "
"the symbols as well. This spesific variant is mostly refered to as sudoku."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a lot of variants, and only one will be discused here. A variant "
"is samurai. This game has 5 9x9 grids, each with 9 3x3 sub grids (so 5 times "
"sudoku). One grid is in the middle and the other 4 are located at its "
"corners, overlapping with the sub-grid located at each corner. The overlap "
"imposes a new constaint because every corner is used twice in a sudoku each "
"demanding the \"all and only once\" rule for each row and column"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting a game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At startup you're presented a list of available sudoku variants. Just select "
"one. Before you hit the play button to start the game, note the difficulty "
"setting at the bottem. The more the slide is set to the right, the more "
"diffucult the game will be."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filling in the blanks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Playing &ksudoku; means you have to insert the correct symbols at the blank "
"squares. Symbol selection can be done with a left click on an symbol located "
"in the grid or located at the sidebar. Inserting a symbol is then a simple "
"right mouse click on a (origanaly) blank square. Or you can use the arrow-"
"keys to move around and alfa-numeric to insert a symbol (the keys are "
"translated to the correct symbol if possible). When inserting a symbol with "
"the keyboard, that symbol will become the selected symbol."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "System guides"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The gui heighlights the column and row the input will go. This makes it "
"easier to see if a symbol already is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When pressing ctrl squares are highlighted which could be a valid place for "
"the current selected symbol. This of course takes a bit fun out of the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you make a mistake, the symbol will be colored red."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are complete stuck, you can ask for a hint. A blank square will be "
"filled as if it was filled from the beginning."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksudoku; keeps a history so you can undo and redo your moves. You can save "
"and load your games and create your own puzzle and even your own sudoku "
"variant!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to create your own puzzle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Start with a empty puzzle. Insert symbols. When satisfied you can use \"check"
"\" to find out if there are more than one, one, or no solutions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to create your own sudoku variant"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
